> inside a box (not that I know of anyway.  Does anyone have a method?).

There are two ways that I can think of offhand.  One way is to lock
the box and then #force it with a blunt weapon, hoping that you
destroy the container.  Of course, once you succeed with the weapon
the lock is broken and you can no longer force it.  Why you can
destroy abox when forcing a lock, but not otherwise, I'm not entirely
sure.  The other way is to find an enemy gelatinous cube and have it
eat and dissolve the box.  When you kill it, the contents will be
there.

I just normally ignore gray stones in boxes.  Luckstones are
guaranteed at the mine end and, although slightly useful, I haven't
ever had a pressing need for a touchstone.

